{
  // SECURITY: role/business_id carry FIELD-LEVEL write RLS locking them to
  // role `admin` — the tier the service role evaluates as (it does NOT bypass
  // RLS; it is evaluated as an admin principal). Without this lock, ANY
  // authenticated user could call auth.updateMe({role:"admin"}) to become a
  // platform-wide admin (every tenant entity carries an unscoped
  // user_condition:{role:"admin"} branch), or updateMe({business_id:"<any id>"})
  // to take over another tenant's data without its invite code. All legitimate
  // changes flow through the service-role functions complete-onboarding and
  // manage-member.
  //
  // DELIBERATELY NO ENTITY-LEVEL "rls" BLOCK — do not add one.
  // The built-in User is not a normal entity; Base44 manages it through the
  // app's authentication system (its own MCP tooling refuses to write it:
  // "Users are managed through the app's authentication system"). An
  // entity-level rls block here does NOT behave like it does on a normal
  // entity — it silently breaks writes to User.
  //
  // This cost a full debugging session to find. Symptom: "Crear negocio" on
  // /onboarding failed with HTTP 500 and a completely EMPTY response body,
  // while Business.create in the very same function succeeded (orphaned
  // Business rows with created_by_id: service_* and nobody attached). The
  // empty body is the tell: a thrown error would have been caught by
  // complete-onboarding's own try/catch and returned as {message}, so the
  // request never returned at all — it hung and the runtime killed it.
  //
  // Mechanism: this entity previously carried an entity-level rls block whose
  // read/update rules included a {{user.data.business_id}} branch. The service
  // principal has NO User row of its own (confirmed: the app has exactly one
  // User record, is_service:false), so that template cannot resolve for it.
  // Business.create kept working because Business's *create* rule is
  // $or[{role:admin},{created_by_id:{{user.id}}}] — no {{user.data.*}} at all,
  // and {{user.id}} comes from the token rather than from an entity read.
  //
  // stockflow — the portfolio's reference standard app, whose equivalent
  // onboarding (business:createBusinessSafe) does the identical
  // asServiceRole.entities.User.update(user.id, {business_id, role}) and
  // works — also carries field-level RLS only, with no entity-level block.
  // Match it. Member listing that needs to span a tenant goes through a
  // service-role function (stockflow's permissions:getTeamMembers), not a
  // client-side entity read gated by RLS on User.
  "name": "User",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "role": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["admin", "business_admin", "staff"],
      "default": "staff",
      "description": "Rol de CtrlHQ (distinto del rol operador de Mission Control: owner|admin|viewer en members). admin = dueño de plataforma ACACIA (rama service-role de RLS); business_admin = dueño/gerente del negocio; staff = personal del negocio.",
      "rls": { "write": { "user_condition": { "role": "admin" } } }
    },
    "business_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Tenant al que pertenece este usuario. Solo lo escriben las Base44 functions complete-onboarding / manage-member (service role) tras validar la invitación — nunca directo desde el cliente, para cerrar el bypass de auth.updateMe.",
      "rls": { "write": { "user_condition": { "role": "admin" } } }
    },
    "pending_business_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Solicitud de unión pendiente (Business.id cuyo invite_code canjeó este usuario). SOLO gobierna la escritura: la escribe complete-onboarding (join / cancel_join) y la limpian manage-member (approve / reject / remove) y delete-account, todas con service role. Bloqueado a role admin porque no concede acceso por sí mismo: ninguna regla RLS lo compara, y el acceso solo nace cuando un business_admin aprueba y manage-member escribe business_id y role. Si se quitara el bloqueo, un usuario podría falsear una solicitud ante un negocio que no le corresponde y engañar al listado de solicitudes de su administrador. Vacío = sin solicitud.",
      "rls": { "write": { "user_condition": { "role": "admin" } } }
    }
  },
  // Matches stockflow: no required fields. `role` carries a default instead, so
  // a brand-new signup is a `staff` with no business until complete-onboarding
  // grants one.
  "required": []
}
